.TH XMRENDERTABLECVTFROMPROP 3 2026-09-14 "Motif 2.6.0"
.SH NAME
XmRenderTableCvtFromProp - Unserialize a render table

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <Xm/Xm.h>

\fBXmRenderTable XmRenderTableCvtFromProp\fR(\fBWidget\fR widget,
\fB                                      \fR \fBchar *\fRproperty,
\fB                                      \fR \fBunsigned int\fR length);
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
This function converts a render table in serialized form back into a
proper render table instance. This faciliatates the transfer of render
tables over the selection by way of the \fB_MOTIF_RENDER_TABLE\fP atom.

.IP "\fIwidget\fP" 12
Widget from whence to get the display, or \fBNULL\fP.
.IP "\fIproperty\fP" 12
Serialized render table.
.IP "\fIlength\fP" 12
Number of bytes in \fIproperty\fP.

.SH RETURN VALUE
A newly-created \fBXmRenderTable\fP or \fBNULL\fP on failure. The resulting
render table must be freed with \fBXmRenderTableFree\fP(3).

.SH HISTORY
This function was introduced in Motif 2.0, and seems to have gone largely
unused. It was neglected, and not updated for Xft support in Motif 2.3.0.
The original implementation serialized the rendertable into a human-readable
string, but in Motif 2.6.0, this has been rewritten to use a TLV-style
binary format.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBXmRendition\fP(3), \fBXmRenderTableCvtToProp\fP(3)

